{
 "description": "Cross-repo pricing parity cases: gross_list, ladder, from_price, order value, value percent, line totals. Amounts are gross RON strings, ROUND_HALF_UP to 2dp. Rules: product rows win outright; else category rows over the product category and its ancestors, best percent per threshold; non-discountable products get no ladder, count toward the order value and receive no value percent (from_price null). Value percent is applied per line on unit_q x qty. Rolling cases add `rolling_rules` (same shape as `rules`, measured against the customer's last 12 months) and `customer` (`rolling_value` in gross RON, `rolling_quantities` per product code). Absent means empty. The two axes compound: 1 - (1-p1)(1-p2), rounded to 2dp once. The quantity axis composes into the unit price; the value axis composes into the per-line percent. A rolling category tier is compared against the quantity accumulated across that category and its descendants, evaluated per chain level against that level's own ladder, best percent winning -- unlike an order-basis category tier, which is compared against the line quantity. `max_rolling_percent` is the highest percent in a product's resolved rolling ladder. `from_price` composes the best tier price with the top order percent, the top rolling order percent and the top rolling quantity percent. A non-discountable product earns no rolling quantity percent and no rolling order-value percent, exactly as it earns none on the order axis, while its line still counts toward the order value.",
